WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:02.738
The answer to check
six: the plan holds it.

2
00:00:02.738 --> 00:00:04.587
Containment stays with a person.

3
00:00:04.587 --> 00:00:06.601
Scene seven asks two things.

4
00:00:06.601 --> 00:00:08.013
Who else did this touch?

5
00:00:08.013 --> 00:00:12.786
The guide's cross-source query finds users
with alerts from more than one sensor in

6
00:00:12.786 --> 00:00:15.313
a week, and an emergency
access account goes

7
00:00:15.313 --> 00:00:17.700
to the top for the incident response lead.

8
00:00:17.700 --> 00:00:19.888
And what may Defender do on its own?

9
00:00:19.888 --> 00:00:22.717
Ring 0's device group
is at full remediation,

10
00:00:22.717 --> 00:00:26.412
so Defender may clean up our
workstation automatically.

11
00:00:26.412 --> 00:00:28.013
A server group never is.

12
00:00:28.013 --> 00:00:32.674
And every emergency access account must
be excluded from attack disruption,

13
00:00:32.674 --> 00:00:35.640
so an incident can't lock
out the people who fix it.
